    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense for May 28th is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries our highest daily efficiency score of 74.75. Facing Bassitt, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.13 xERA matchup and a significant park factor boost, making him our primary engine for runs and RBI. **Gunnar Henderson** follows closely with a 71.81 score; despite a minor penalty for facing a lefty in Corbin, **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s elite base projection and favorable batting order placement keep him as a must-start staple for our daily production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves the utility slot and the bench. **Coby Mayo** earns a start with a 66.72 score, as his dynamic platoon advantage against the lefty Corbin outweighs the static projections of others. This pushed **Miguel Vargas** to the bench with a 60.21 score; while **Miguel Vargas** remains a strong asset, he narrowly missed the cut because his matchup against Woods Richardson lacked the specific platoon upside that **Coby Mayo** provides. Meanwhile, **Josh Jung** (63.10) rounds out the starting five, benefiting from a soft matchup against Arrighetti, providing a high-floor option that edges out the remainder of our reserve corps.\n\nRisk management remains a priority for the Waves as we navigate this mid-week slate. While we are maximizing our output, we are mindful of the \"Elite Hold\" penalty applied to **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** due to the specific defensive profiles of their opposition, which slightly dampens their stolen base potential\u2014the most critical metric in our 5x5 Roto chase. With **Luis Robert Jr.** continuing to occupy an IL spot and **Kyle Tucker** off the schedule, we are operating with a tightened bench. We have effectively purged low-upside contributors like **Dominic Smith** (39.63), whose sub-40 score correctly keeps him sidelined to preserve our remaining game caps for higher-leverage situations in the coming weekend series.",
